    "long_instructions": "## Do This:\r\n\r\nFollow the instructions in the **Document Design Flaws** section of your [Interactivity in Web Apps](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AtRRufIl4mUbldpHK-seyaVGiGvaUAX3IZwcpw7Ymgo/edit?usp=sharing) activity guide.\r\n",
    "name_suffix": "_-js-2026",
    "ai_tutor_prompt_settings": {
      "answerTypes": [
        "ask"
      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "ask": "Students are exploring two versions of a web app and comparing how the interactions affect the user experience. Ask questions that prompt them to identify what feels confusing or helpful when they interact with the app, but do not explain the issues or tell them which version is better."
      }
    },
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "Design guide \r\n\r\n**Making Parts Interactive**\r\n1. Explore the web app: Try the buttons and input to see what happens.\r\n   \r\n2. Look for parts: List as many elements (parts of the page) as you can in the box below. Then, circle or highlight the ones that could change (for example, an image could change).\r\n\r\n3. Choose an interaction: Pick ONE button or input and tell the AI to make it work. Include the name of the button or input (\"Show Message\" or \"Next Image\"), what the user does (click, type), and what is supposed to happen (show a new message, display the next image, etc).\r\nBefore you prompt the AI, complete this sentence:\r\nWhen the user ____________________ on the ______________________, the page should ____________________________.\r\n\r\n4. Test the event: Test the interaction. Does it work the way you expected?\r\n\r\n   \r\n**Document Design Flaws**\r\n\r\nTry to use the web app. Then, go to the next level to explore and use a similar web app. \r\n- As you use each app, pay attention to:\r\n- What happens when you select buttons or type\r\n- What feels confusing, inconsistent, or frustrating\r\n- Which version was better? What made the better version easier or more helpful to use? \r\n\r\n**Quick Design Sprint**\r\n\r\nDo This: Who is your user? Be specific! Draw or describe what you would change to improve the app.\r\n\r\n- How does your change help the user?\r\n- Could your change make anything harder for someone else?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "widget2": {
      "id": "remindme-1"
    }
  },
